VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-18T23:23:45Z","updated_at":"2025-05-18T23:24:41Z","body":"> [@Calinou](https://github.com/Calinou) do you have any insight on this?\n\nThere are several issues on particle interpolation. The closest are probably https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/77916 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/72919. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/84227 may also be related.\n\n> and i've been working around them by increasing the FixedFps setting to 120 or 240, but I don't know if this is a safe workaround moving forward and if there is a bug here in the engine.\n\nIt's fine to do in my experience. If your particles don't use trails, you can also set it to `0` and disable **Interpolate** so the particles simulate every rendered frame. (Trails require fixed FPS by design; they will fall back to 30 FPS if Fixed FPS is `0`.)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2889271039/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]